R-C16 R-C15 R-C9 R-C14 R-IN2 (slice 085, needs slice 082: the notes of the resolve for a young release that a pattern keeps): `tln init --platform acme/pfv` with `acme/*` in `config.toml`. `acme/pfv` has 1.1.0 (old), 1.2.0 (30 hours old) and 1.3.0 (1 day old). Run x5: the start release is 1.3.0 (young, kept by the pattern). The fake unit check fails 1.3.0 on every compiler, so the resolve moves the platform to 1.2.0, which is young and kept by the pattern too. There is no note for the start release 1.3.0 (it is not in the header at the end). There is the note of slice 082 for the release that is in the header: `note: pf 1.2.0 is 1d old (min-release-age 2d), not hidden by min-release-age-exclude: acme/*` (the id is the alias, as in the R-C7 note). This case passes only with the code of slice 082.
